{
  "description": "Diagnosis of where the Stage-1 reply draft is lost on the Pixel 10a (app versionCode 39, resident at elizaOS/eliza c35106fb14). A temporary logging copy of files/agent/agent-bundle.js (stock sha256 4840ce3e4f958e80a540a606b5311bd658bcbe2ae66f286776ae25c4770edb48) logged sizes, field names, gate inputs, timings and at most 80 characters of reply text to a private JSONL file; no headers, tokens, keys or prompts. Six typed direct questions were sent through the chat composer over CDP. The stock bundle was then restored byte-identical (sha256 verified on the device), the diagnostic log deleted, the agent restarted with Settings > Agent > Restart agent, and the health check passed. ipc-recovery slots stayed at 6 of 8 through the diagnosis.",
  "recordedAt": "2026-11-06",
  "upstreamPin": "c35106fb14003a5a85e9793dabcf047118cc09e0",
  "sourceMapped": "/home/shaw/.cache/alphaphone-voice-36236fc/eliza-stream at c35106fb14",
  "findings": [
    {
      "where": "Stage-1 stream gate: plugins/plugin-assistant/src/services/message/stage1-reply-stream.ts (REQUIRED_WHEN_EMITTED_FIELDS), fed by stage1-decision.ts:764-768 (activeResponseHandlerFields) and :845 (createStage1DirectReplyStreamGate(activeResponseHandlerFields))",
      "evidence": "Every gate call was denied although all preceding values were direct-answer values (RESPOND, [simple], [], none, [], Notes read_only or unresolved with no operations, navigation none). The emitted-field list the gate receives contains contextRequests, which is not in the HANDLE_RESPONSE tool schema the model received: stage1-decision.ts:586 applies withAvailableContextRequests(fieldSchema, discovery.available), which deletes contextRequests when no references are available (context-discovery.ts:177-189). activeResponseHandlerFields removes only skippedFieldNames, so the gate requires a field the model was never offered. Logged reason on both instrumented turns: missing-emitted:contextRequests.",
      "effect": "The extractor holds the attempt at passesGate; no chunk reaches downstreamChunk, chat-routes onStreamChunk is never called, and the conversation route writes only the final non-provisional snapshot.",
      "recommendedFix": "stage1-decision.ts:845: build the gate from the fields actually present in the emitted HANDLE_RESPONSE schema, e.g. filter activeResponseHandlerFields() by Object.hasOwn(<schema given to the HANDLE_RESPONSE tool>.properties, field.name), capturing that schema where referenceSchema/createMessageHandlerTools is built (about lines 470-590, rebuilt at 1540). Leave activeResponseHandlerFields itself unchanged because it also feeds the local grammar. Add a reply-stream-gate test where contextRequests is selected but removed by withAvailableContextRequests."
    },
    {
      "where": "Eliza Cloud chat/completions stream as read by plugins/plugin-elizacloud/src/models/text.ts streamNativeChatCompletion generate()",
      "evidence": "Every Stage-1 call had three choice frames: an empty tool-call arguments delta 507-1067 ms after the body started, the complete HANDLE_RESPONSE arguments (336-726 characters) in one delta 0-2 ms later, and finish_reason tool_calls 4-17 ms after that. No delta.content and no aggregated re-send. streamReplyToolArgs was true and the plugin yielded the whole envelope as one chunk.",
      "effect": "With the gate fixed, the draft would still arrive as one provisional chunk a few milliseconds before the final reply, so voice could not start meaningfully earlier.",
      "recommendedFix": "Determine whether the Cloud gateway chat/completions route or the Cerebras upstream buffers tool-call arguments, and forward argument deltas as they are generated. The client side (text.ts accumulateToolCallDeltas, lowestIndexToolCallArgs, yield of the suffix) already handles incremental deltas."
    },
    {
      "where": "packages/core/src/runtime/model-dispatch.ts deliverModelStreamChunk (GuardedStreamScanner)",
      "evidence": "A secret/PII guard session was active on every call; it released the envelope minus its last 79-98 characters until flush.",
      "effect": "Secondary: it trims the tail of a streamed chunk until flush; relevant only after the two issues above are fixed."
    }
  ],
